/-! # Left exactness of coefficient reduction for a projective symmetric presentation

Source: Stacks Project, Smoothing Ring Maps, proof of Tag 07CE, equation-sequence;
More on Algebra, Tags 07CX and 07D4.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open scoped TensorProduct

namespace Algebra

/-- Source: Stacks Project, Smoothing Ring Maps, proof of Tag 07CE, lines 357–414,
and More on Algebra, proof of Tag 07D4 via Tag 07CX.
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-projective-symmetric-conormal-reduction-exact)

Proof. Write `A = P/I`, `M = I/I²`, `C = Sym_A(M)`, `Q = P[y]`,
`B = A[y]`, `H = IQ`, `J = ker φ`, and `L = ker α`. Coefficient reduction
`Q → B` is surjective with kernel `H`. The compatibility of `φ` and `α` gives
`H ≤ J` and `J/H = L`. It induces a surjection `r : J/J² → L/L²` whose kernel
is the image of `H/(H ∩ J²)`: indeed, `L²` is the image of `J²` under reduction.
The split surjection `q` makes `M` and `ker q` finite projective. Choose a common
finite principal-open free cover of `A` and lift its elements to `P`. In adapted
coordinates on each nonempty member, `B → C` is `A_a[u,v] → A_a[u]`, so `L` is
generated by the regular sequence of complementary variables `v`. The regular
quotient intersection theorem gives `H ∩ J² = HJ` on that member. The quotient
`(H ∩ J²)/HJ` is a `C`-module; its localizations vanish, so the unit-ideal cover
implies `H ∩ J² = HJ` globally. Zero members have zero modules and cause no exception.
Since the polynomial algebra `Q` is free over `P`, coefficient expansion identifies
`H` with `Q ⊗_P I`. Quotienting by `JH` gives
`H/HJ = C ⊗_P I = C ⊗_A (I/I²)`, since `I` kills `C`. Explicitly, this
isomorphism sends `c ⊗ [x]` to the class of a lift of `c` times `C(x)`;
changing the lifts changes this by `HJ`. Its inverse expands an element of `H`
coefficientwise and reduces each coefficient modulo `I²` and each monomial under `φ`.
Together with `H ∩ J² = HJ`, this yields the injective map `i` with image `ker r`.
The displayed formulas are precisely inclusion and coefficient reduction on kernel
representatives. When `A = 0`, `C` and all the displayed modules are zero, so the
same conclusions hold. -/
theorem projective_symmetric_conormal_reduction_exact
    (P : Type u) [CommRing P] (I : Ideal P) (m : ℕ)
    [Module.Projective (P ⧸ I) I.Cotangent]
    (q : (Fin m → P ⧸ I) →ₗ[P ⧸ I] I.Cotangent) (hq : Function.Surjective q)
    (α : MvPolynomial (Fin m) (P ⧸ I) →ₐ[P ⧸ I] SymmetricAlgebra (P ⧸ I) I.Cotangent)
    (hαX : ∀ j, α (MvPolynomial.X j) =
      SymmetricAlgebra.ι (P ⧸ I) I.Cotangent (q (Pi.single j 1)))
    (φ : MvPolynomial (Fin m) P →+* SymmetricAlgebra (P ⧸ I) I.Cotangent)
    (hφeq : φ = α.toRingHom.comp (MvPolynomial.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)))
    (hφ : Function.Surjective φ) (hα : Function.Surjective α) :
    ∃ (i : SymmetricAlgebra (P ⧸ I) I.Cotangent ⊗[P ⧸ I] I.Cotangent
        →ₗ[SymmetricAlgebra (P ⧸ I) I.Cotangent]
          (Extension.ofSurjective φ.toIntAlgHom hφ).Cotangent)
      (r : (Extension.ofSurjective φ.toIntAlgHom hφ).Cotangent
        →ₗ[SymmetricAlgebra (P ⧸ I) I.Cotangent] (Extension.ofSurjective α hα).Cotangent),
      (∀ (c : SymmetricAlgebra (P ⧸ I) I.Cotangent) (x : I)
        (y : (Extension.ofSurjective φ.toIntAlgHom hφ).ker),
        y.1 = MvPolynomial.C x.1 →
          i (c ⊗ₜ I.toCotangent x) = c • Extension.Cotangent.mk y) ∧
      (∀ (x : (Extension.ofSurjective φ.toIntAlgHom hφ).ker)
        (y : (Extension.ofSurjective α hα).ker),
        y.1 = MvPolynomial.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) x.1 →
          r (Extension.Cotangent.mk x) = Extension.Cotangent.mk y) ∧
      Function.Injective i ∧ Function.Exact i r ∧ Function.Surjective r := by sorry

end Algebra
